#. Tag: title
#: tips.docbook:8
#, no-c-format
msgid "Useful tips"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tips.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid "Reading documentation in &kde;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tips.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Pop up the <guilabel>Run Command</guilabel> window (<keycombo action=\"simul"
"\">&Alt;<keycap>F2</keycap></keycombo> by default) and type:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tips.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>man:<replaceable>command</replaceable></command> for man pages. It "
"even unpacks on the fly if the man pages are gzipped."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tips.docbook:26
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>info:<replaceable>command</replaceable></command> for info pages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tips.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>help:<replaceable>kdeappname</replaceable></command> for &kde; "
"application help pages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tips.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also enter any of these in the <guilabel>Location</guilabel> text "
"box in &konqueror;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tips.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Or you can use the <application>&kde; Help Center</application> if you are "
"using &kde; 2. Simply start the <application>&kde; Help Center</application> "
"by clicking on the icon (the blue book with the yellow key) on the toolbar. "
"Once the <application>&kde; Help Center</application> has loaded, the window "
"on the left will contain an entry called <guilabel>Unix manual pages</"
"guilabel>. Click once on this entry, and you can browse through all the "
"installed manual pages on your system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tips.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid "Move or resize windows quickly"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tips.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To move a window, use <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;<mousebutton>left</"
"mousebutton></keycombo> mouse button. <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;"
"<mousebutton>right</mousebutton></keycombo> mouse button will resize the "
"window. Last but not least, <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;"
"<mousebutton>middle</mousebutton></keycombo> mouse button raises/lowers the "
"window. The <application>&kde; Control Center</application> allows you to "
"change these mouse bindings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tips.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid "Killing windows in &kde;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tips.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is a standard keybinding (<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Alt;&Esc;</"
"keycombo>) that gives you a skull &amp; crossbones cursor. Click that cursor "
"on a window to kill it. The keybindings are viewable/changeable from the "
"<application>&kde; Control Center</application>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tips.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using this option kills the program forcibly. Data may be lost, and some "
"processes related to the program may remain active. Use only as a last "
"resort."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tips.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"What if something is so wrong that I can't even get the skull &amp; "
"crossbones cursor? How do I get out of a total lockup?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tips.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These kind of locks tend to occur when an application locks up while it has "
"a so called <quote>mouse/keyboard grab</quote>. When that happens you can "
"try to select a virtual text console with <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;"
"&Alt;<keycap>F1</keycap></keycombo> and login. With the following command "
"you will get a list of all running processes:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: tips.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>        <command>ps</command> <option>-aux</option> | "
"<command>more</command></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tips.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By killing the process that has the mousegrab, your desktop will come to "
"life again. Unfortunately you can't see which process that is, so you will "
"have to find out through trial and error. To kill a process use:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: tips.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>        <command>kill</command> <option>-9</option> "
"<replaceable>pid</replaceable></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tips.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here <replaceable>pid</replaceable> is the process id of the process, which "
"is the first number on each line reported by <command>ps</command> <option>-"
"aux</option>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tips.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can switch back to the desktop with <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;"
"&Alt;<keycap>F7</keycap></keycombo> (or <keycap>F8</keycap> through "
"<keycap>F9</keycap> depending on your operating system) to see if things "
"work again. When you press <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;<keycap>Tab</"
"keycap></keycombo> you should get a response from the window manager. If "
"not, you need to get back to the text console and try to kill another "
"process."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tips.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Good candidates to kill are: the application you were working with, "
"&kicker;, &klipper; and &kdesktop;."
msgstr ""
